## Context
Missing work the implementation review surfaced (panel/cycle2/
review-implementation.md §5.1): X5 gates scoped issue B (0034, which
supersedes the RFC 0027) on the segmenter's measured precision, and seg/1
had no implementation anywhere — days of new code standing between 0025's X5
and 0034, priced nowhere until now. The spec lives once, in DESIGN.md §2.2;
build to it, not to a paraphrase. Political-review checkpoint applies: check zotero#6012's state
before building — structured extraction landing upstream makes heuristic
segmentation a fallback at best (panel/cycle2/review-political.md finding 5).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] #6012 checkpoint recorded here before implementation starts
- [ ] seg/1 runnable over flat /fulltext text, emitting entries + confidence
- [ ] deterministic on fixture text; identity string (seg/1) for the chunker key
- [ ] X5 (0025) can consume it on the author's machine
